    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d212">

                <pb facs="0182" n="178" xml:id="pg178"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.811/1006: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-08-30T13:00:00+09:00">August 30, 1938—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 30—6:44 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>566. Embassy’s 557, August 26, noon,<anchor n="34" xml:id="d212-f1"/> Whangpoo
                    Conservancy. Separate but similar signed notes substantially embodying the text
                    mentioned in paragraph 1 of Shanghai’s 1152, August 22, 7 p.m., have been
                    submitted to the Foreign Minister by the British, French and American Embassies
                    under date of August 29.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Shanghai.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
